  "religion": {
    "_note": "Deity-names are the Frankish-branch reflexes of the common-Germanic theonym ancestors (family_germanic.json), with Anglo-Saxon-overlay variants in the eastern shires - phoneme-morphs of the Agrippan canon, never real Germanic gods. Lawful/Neutral henotheist: the One above His ministers; Neutral folk keep the saints and the hallowed dead at the minster.",
